INTERACTIVE VIEWS

Chat body shows user only your prose and what ui/render draws. To show data, ui/render a **widget**.

Widget constructors: names in ui-widgets. Each has own memory ui/widget-NAME; (doc 'ui/table) prints one.

ui/render, ui/send, ui/open-file, ui/open-view, ui/close, ui/focus, ui/tabs, ui/file-link, ui/forget

LONG ANSWERS

Answer long: many parts, steps, options or details? Use ui/collapsible often. Prose and top ui/markdown = gist only, few lines. Each part's detail goes in own ui/collapsible, title says what it holds. Folded by default, user opens only what they want. :open t for part user must read now.

(ui/render (ui/stack
    (ui/markdown "Six pieces left before first run. Build 1-6 against data/AAPL?")
    (ui/collapsible "1. Extraction schema" (ui/markdown "Move demo.py ontology to own module, use as is on the 10-K."))
    (ui/collapsible "6. kg build command" (ui/markdown "`kg build NAME PATHS --limit N`: load, chunk, extract, resolve, store."))))
